  e2 [verified, public, as of 2026-06-01T00:00:00-05:00] The registrar does not release an official transcript while a financial hold flag is set on the student's record. Osei's record carries a financial hold for an unpaid balance of $1,842. (source: Registrar policy R-12; student account record)
  e3 [verified, public, as of 2026-06-04T14:00:00-05:00] The financial hold flag on a student record can be lifted only by the bursar's automated reconciliation batch. Registrar staff have no ability to clear or override the flag and the registrar's system contains no manual override. The registrar confirmed this in writing on 4 June 2026 to Osei's advisor, Dr. Kwesi Amankwah, in reply to his request that the release be expedited. (source: Registrar's reply to Dr. Amankwah, 2026-06-04; registrar system administration guide)
  e4 [verified, public, as of 2026-06-01T00:00:00-05:00] The bursar's reconciliation batch runs at 2:00 AM America/Chicago on Tuesdays, Wednesdays, Thursdays and Fridays. It does not run on Saturdays, on Sundays, or on Mondays. This schedule has been unchanged since 2023 and no change is planned for June 2026. (source: Bursar's system operations schedule)
  e5 [verified, public, as of 2026-06-01T00:00:00-05:00] Each run of the batch posts every payment that the university's payment processor has marked cleared and that has not already been posted, and lifts the financial hold on any record whose balance is thereby brought to zero. (source: Bursar's system operations manual, sec. 3)
  e6 [verified, public, as of 2026-06-01T00:00:00-05:00] Wexford State's payment portal accepts electronic checks only. It has not accepted card payments since March 2026, and the cashier's window that accepted certified checks and cash closed permanently in 2025. No other channel exists for paying a student balance. (source: Bursar's office published payment options)
  e7 [verified, public, as of 2026-06-01T00:00:00-05:00] The payment processor's rule is that an electronic check submitted on a processor business day before 5:00 PM is marked cleared at 6:00 PM America/Chicago on the third processor business day following the day of submission. The processor's business days are Monday through Friday, and the processor observes no holidays in June 2026. (source: Payment processor service terms, sec. 5; processor 2026 holiday calendar)
